# User Features (`app/user.py`)

## Saved Filter Profiles (`/user/profiles`)

Allows users to save and restore named dashboard filter configurations.

### API
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/profiles` | GET | Page render |
| `/user/profiles/list?show_all=0` | GET | JSON list, ordered `is_starred DESC, name ASC`; super admin can pass `show_all=1` |
| `/user/profiles/save` | POST JSON | `{name, filter_data}` — filter_data is the full dashboard filter state dict |
| `/user/profiles/<id>/data` | GET | Returns `{id, name, filter_data}` for restoring on dashboard |
| `/user/profiles/<id>` | DELETE | Owner or super admin only |
| `/user/profiles/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` |
| `/user/profiles/<id>/star` | POST JSON | `{is_starred: bool}` — toggle if omitted |

### filter_data JSON structure
Same keys as the dashboard filter form: `subject`, `source_type`, `years`, `topics`, `subtopics`, `chapters`, `levels`, `q_type`, `qid_search`, `sort_config`, etc.

The dashboard JS serialises the current form state into this blob when saving, and restores it by re-populating the filter form when loading.

## Saved Generation Presets (`/user/gen-profiles`)

Reusable generation-option templates. **Options only** — never store `question_ids` or `filter_data`.

Backed by `SavedGenerationProfile` (user_id, name, options_data JSON, is_starred, created_at, updated_at).

### API
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/gen-profiles` | GET | Page render (`saved_gen_profiles.html`) |
| `/user/gen-profiles/list?show_all=0` | GET | JSON list, ordered `is_starred DESC, name ASC` |
| `/user/gen-profiles/save` | POST JSON | `{name, options_data}` — upsert by `(user_id, name)`; `question_ids` is stripped server-side |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>/data` | GET | `{id, name, is_starred, options_data}` for restoring on Generate page |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>` | DELETE | Owner or super admin only |
| `/user/gen-profiles/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` |
| `/user/gen-profiles/<id>/star` | POST JSON | `{is_starred: bool}` — toggle if omitted |

### options_data JSON structure
Same shape as `GeneratedFile.generation_options` (see [document-generation.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/document-generation.mdc)) minus `question_ids`.

The Generate-page JS (`getCurrentGenerationOptions()` in `templates/generate.html`) builds this dict by reading every option control, and `restoreGenerationOptions()` applies it back. Loading a preset never touches the hidden `question_ids`, `sort_config`, or `filter_data` form inputs bound to the current selection.

### Starring
Both `SavedFilter` and `SavedGenerationProfile` have an `is_starred` boolean column (indexed). List endpoints return starred items first; the Generate-page dropdown groups them under a `★ Starred` optgroup.

## My Generated Files (`/user/files`)

Tracks all documents generated by background threads.

### API
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/user/files` | GET | Page render |
| `/user/files/list?show_all=0` | GET | JSON list of `GeneratedFile` records |
| `/user/files/<id>/filter` | GET | Get saved filter_data for "Re-filter" button |
| `/user/files/<id>/generation_options` | GET | Get saved generation_options + display_name for re-generate |
| `/user/files/<id>` | DELETE | Deletes DB record + file from OUTPUT_PATH |
| `/user/files/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids: []}` |

### GeneratedFile status lifecycle
`pending` → `generating` → `completed` | `failed`

The My Files page polls itself every **5 seconds** when any row has `status-generating` class, stopping once all are done.

### Access control
- Owners can access their own files
- Super admins can access all files via `show_all=1`
- View-only users (`can_generate() == False`) cannot access the My Files page at all (403)
